# Design System

Single source of truth for the HOSSPI HMS visual system, built on Material 3.

## Requirements

- Provide comprehensive light, dark, and system themes with semantic status tones, spacing, radius, elevation, and typography via tokens/extensions.
- Light theme is default (blue-based palette); dark theme stays readable and Material-aligned.
- Must not hard-code color, spacing, radius, elevation, or typography in feature or shared widgets.
- Surfaces must remain readable on mobile, tablet, and desktop ([`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc)).
- Reusable theme-aware components must live in `frontend/lib/shared/`.
- Localize all user-facing text; theme changes must update reactively.

## Token access

```dart
final theme = Theme.of(context);
theme.spacing.md;           // AppSpacingTokens
theme.appTokens;            // AppDesignTokens
theme.colorScheme.primary;  // ColorScheme roles
```

- Use `theme.textTheme` for typography, not inline `TextStyle`.
- Use semantic status tones from theme extensions, not ad-hoc `Colors.green`.

## Tokens

| Group | Values |
|---|---|
| Spacing | `xs=4`, `sm=8`, `md=12`, `lg=16`, `xl=24`, `xxl=32` |
| Radius | `xs=4` … `xxl=24`, `full=pill` (open scale, no cap) |
| Page padding | mobile `16`, tablet `24`, desktop `32` |
| Icon size | `20–24`; larger only when required |

## Shape

- Source radii from `theme.radius`; make them responsive via `context.responsiveRadius(...)`.
- Rely on `BorderRadius` auto-clamping; keep shape language uniform across cards, buttons, dialogs.

